(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[13 1 "// Interp is an interpreter (PyInterpreterState): its builtins, its modules (sys.modules), its standard"] [14 1 "// streams and its recursion limit."] [21 2 "// replExit is the SystemExit that ended the REPL's loop (replLoop), which sys._baserepl raises on (queue 298)"] [23 2 "// displaying is set while traceback's display runs (displayByTraceback): an error displayed meanwhile takes the Go"] [24 2 "// display"] [26 2 "// xi is the interpreter's state for PEP 734 (interpreters.go, queue 230)"] [28 2 "// sysMod is the interpreter's sys module (interp->sysdict's), kept when sys.modules no longer has it (queue 253)"] [30 2 "// builtinsCopy is interp->builtins_copy, the builtins finalize_modules restores (queue 253)"] [32 2 "// finalPhase is the end's progress (pylifecycle.go, queue 253): 0 running, 1 finalizing (sys.is_finalizing()),"] [33 2 "// 2 the modules out of sys.modules (imports fail, no source lines in tracebacks)"] [35 2 "// final is what the end keeps of the warnings module (_warnings' state)"] [39 1 "// NewInterp is a fresh interpreter writing to stdout and stderr."] [52 1 "// startXOptions are the -X options of the command line (queue 220): bin/pyi python passes them in PYI_XOPTIONS, one"] [53 1 "// per line, NAME or NAME=VALUE; read once and removed from the environment (a child of the program does not inherit"] [54 1 "// them, as -X is not inherited)."] [74 1 "// startEnv is os.Getenv of a PYTHON* variable at start: \"\" under -E or -I (bin/pyi python's PYI_IGNORE_ENV, read once"] [75 1 "// and removed from the environment as PYI_XOPTIONS is)."] [92 2 "// atStartHooks run before the main module (Py_InitializeMain's late steps: queue 220, faulthandler's enable for"] [93 2 "// -X faulthandler and PYTHONFAULTHANDLER); an error is printed and the run's status is 1"] [97 1 "// startFlag reports a command-line option of bin/pyi python's PYI_START_FLAGS (queue 296, read once and removed from the"] [98 1 "// environment as PYI_INSPECT is): 'q' for -q, 'E' for -E, 'I' for -I; sys.flags' quiet, ignore_environment and"] [99 1 "// isolated (asyncio's REPL reads quiet for its banner and ignore_environment for PYTHONSTARTUP)."] [113 1 "// startInspect is -i (bin/pyi python's PYI_INSPECT, queue 289, read once and removed from the environment as"] [114 1 "// PYI_SAFE_PATH is): 0 without it, 1 for -i, 2 for -i with no code to run (CPython's REPL on stdin, its banner but"] [115 1 "// under -q), and 2 or 3 too for no code on a terminal without -i (queue 313, pymain_run_stdin's stdin_is_interactive:"] [116 1 "// startInspectOption false). PYTHONINSPECT at start (but under -E or -I) sets sys.flags.inspect, not interactive, as"] [117 1 "// config's inspect."] [142 2 "// inspectTTY: the REPL is the run because stdin is a terminal, not -i (sys.flags' inspect and interactive 0)"] [146 1 "// startInspectOption is whether -i was given (config's inspect and interactive)."] [149 1 "// inspectAfter is pymain_repl's test (Modules/main.c): the REPL after the main module when -i was given or"] [150 1 "// PYTHONINSPECT is set (at start, or in the environment the program leaves), stdin a terminal or -i given."] [159 1 "// endMain is the main module's end with its status: Py_FinalizeEx's, or under -i the REPL on stdin in __main__'s"] [160 1 "// namespace (pymain_repl; the module's exception, SystemExit's too, printed before it), whose status is the run's."] [169 2 "// pymain_set_inspect(config, 0) before the REPL: sys.flags.inspect 0 in it (sys made first: an empty main module"] [170 2 "// has not made it)"] [176 3 "// no code to run: the REPL is the run, its __main__ the empty stdin module's without a __file__"] [178 3 "// and with what pylifecycle's add_main_module gives it (queue 298, test_pyrepl's globals tests): __package__ and"] [179 3 "// __spec__ None, __loader__ importlib's BuiltinImporter"] [184 21 "// stderr unbuffered, as CPython's: the banner before the hook's and _pyrepl's imports (queue 298)"] [191 2 "// sys.__interactivehook__ (pymain_run_interactive_hook; queue 298: site's register_readline, the history file)"] [195 2 "// on a terminal, _pyrepl (pymain_run_pyrepl; queue 298): pythonstartup after code (pymain_repl), not on stdin's run"] [196 2 "// (pymain_run_stdin ran the startup file above)"] [203 1 "// mainModuleDefaults gives __main__'s namespace g of a run with no code the names CPython's __main__ starts with"] [204 1 "// (add_main_module, Python/pylifecycle.c): __package__ and __spec__ None, __loader__ BuiltinImporter, each when absent."] [226 1 "// runInteractiveHook is pymain_run_interactive_hook (Modules/main.c; queue 298), before the REPL: sys.__interactivehook__"] [227 1 "// called when sys has one (site's register_readline: readline's or _pyrepl's history file read, its write at exit"] [228 1 "// registered); an error is \"Failed calling sys.__interactivehook__\" and printed, the session going on, but SystemExit,"] [229 1 "// whose status ends the run (exit true), as pymain_err_print."] [234 2 "// site, which CPython imports at start (pyi does not): imported here, before the REPL, so that its main sets the hook"] [235 2 "// (enablerlcompleter, but under -I)"] [259 1 "// runStartup is pymain_run_startup (Modules/main.c; queue 293), before the REPL on stdin when there is no code to run:"] [260 1 "// the file PYTHONSTARTUP names (not under -E or -I) run in __main__'s namespace g as _PyRun_SimpleFileObject runs it,"] [261 1 "// its __file__ set for the run, an error printed (sys.excepthook) and the session going on; SystemExit ends the run"] [262 1 "// with its status (exit true), as PyErr_Print's handle_system_exit; a file that does not open: \"Could not open"] [263 1 "// PYTHONSTARTUP\" and its OSError printed."] [306 1 "// cModeFile is the file bin/pyi python writes -c's code into (queue 220): run as CPython runs -c, its code's file"] [307 1 "// \"<string>\", no __file__, sys.path[0] \"\"."] [310 1 "// mModeFile and stdinModeFile are the files bin/pyi python writes for -m and for a program read from stdin (queue 250)."] [316 1 "// startSafePath is -P (safe_path) as bin/pyi python's command line gave it (PYI_SAFE_PATH: 1 under -P or -I, 0"] [317 1 "// without, read once and removed from the environment as PYI_IGNORE_ENV is); -1 when not run by bin/pyi python (bin/pyi"] [318 1 "// run's programs and the check's driver, whose sys.flags.safe_path is the reference driver's -P)."] [339 1 "// ExecModule runs a module's code object as the module name (its namespace's __name__), returning"] [340 1 "// the module, or the uncaught exception."] [345 1 "// PrintException writes an uncaught exception as CPython's default excepthook does"] [346 1 "// (Lib/traceback.py's format): the chain first (__cause__, else __context__ unless suppressed), each"] [347 1 "// with its traceback (the file, line and function, and the source line when the file reads) and"] [348 1 "// \"Type: text\", a SyntaxError's location and caret, the notes. Carets under expressions are not"] [349 1 "// printed (PY5b: a recorded difference)."] [350 1 "//"] [351 1 "// The text goes to sys.stderr (PyErr_Display's file): the process's standard error while sys.stderr is"] [352 1 "// the one it started with, else the text is written by sys.stderr.write and flushed (support.captured_stderr),"] [353 1 "// nothing when sys.stderr is None or missing, write's errors ignored."] [367 1 "// PrintUncaught is PyErr_Print (Python/pythonrun.c's _PyErr_PrintEx with set_sys_last_vars, queue 223): an uncaught"] [368 1 "// exception, not SystemExit, stored as sys.last_exc, last_type, last_value and last_traceback, then given to"] [369 1 "// sys.excepthook(type, value, traceback); \"sys.excepthook is missing\" and the display when it is absent or None; when"] [370 1 "// the hook raises, \"Error in sys.excepthook:\", that error's display, then \"Original exception was:\" and the original's."] [377 22 "// after the main module's run: the hook runs on the main thread"] [405 1 "// registerCode is run_mod's interactive source (Python/pythonrun.c, queue 223): -c's code and its nested code objects"] [406 1 "// registered by linecache._register_code(code, source, name), so traceback's display shows -c's lines; an error dropped."] [420 1 "// displayByTraceback is _PyErr_Display's first way (Python/pythonrun.c, queue 223): the stdlib's"] [421 1 "// traceback._print_exception_bltin(exc), Lib/traceback.py's display with its caret lines (PEP 657's positions,"] [422 1 "// co_positions), chains, groups and notes; false when the module or its function is missing or the call raised (the"] [423 1 "// error dropped, as PyErr_Clear), the caller then printing the Go display (print_exception_recursive's fallback)."] [424 1 "// Not while traceback itself is being imported or displaying (a second error then printed by the fallback)."] [456 1 "// writeStderr writes text to sys.stderr: in.Stderr when it is the original stream."] [496 4 "// at shutdown CPython's display reads no source (the import of io fails: queue 253)"] [505 1 "// FormatExceptionOnly is traceback.format_exception_only's text: a SyntaxError's location, source"] [506 1 "// line and caret, then \"Type: text\" (the type qualified by its module unless builtins), then the notes."] [511 23 "// traceback's stype: the module unless __main__ or builtins"] [515 3 "// str(exc) (traceback's _safe_string): a class's own __str__"] [595 1 "// RegisterSource gives sourceLine the text of a source that is no file (\"<stdin>\", \"<string>\"): the"] [596 1 "// REPL's statements, as linecache keeps them (PY5e's REQUEST, part 2a). A later text replaces it."] [601 1 "// sourceLine is the stripped text of line n of the file, \"\" when it does not read (linecache)."] [623 1 "// RunModule reads a module's IR (arbace.python.compile's code object as pr-str prints it) and runs it"] [624 1 "// as __main__ with file as __file__, on the process's stdout and stderr; the exit status: 0, 1 for an"] [625 1 "// uncaught exception (its traceback on stderr), SystemExit's code. bin/pyi run calls it."] [626 1 "// mainSourceError is the main file's decoding error as the tokenizer reports a file it reads, the file named"] [627 1 "// (helpers.c's \" in file FILE\", as arbace.python.run/error-answer gives pyi on goi's; queue 284: the compiled"] [628 1 "// launcher's main module, which RunModule decodes): nil when its bytes decode."] [652 2 "// ir is the compiler's answer when the main module does not compile (queue 223): its SyntaxError raised as"] [653 2 "// compile() raises it and given to sys.excepthook, as CPython's pymain_run_file reports it"] [657 37 "// the reader's warnings, emitted once the interpreter stands (queue 228)"] [662 3 "// the coding spec is a codec of Python's the host has no charset for: decoded and compiled below"] [673 2 "// sys.path[0] as CPython's config computes sys_path_0 (sys is made from configPath on its first use; queue 250):"] [674 2 "// none under -P (safe_path), \"\" for -c and stdin, the working directory for -m, else the script's directory"] [749 4 "// a file's parser has no source string (tok->str NULL): _metadata's source None, traceback reads the file"] [764 3 "// -c's sys.path[0] \"\" (none under -P: the first entry is then the standard library's; queue 250)"] [779 22 "// handle_system_exit drops the exception before Py_FinalizeEx"] [792 2 "// Py_FinalizeEx (pylifecycle.go, queue 253): threading._shutdown, the atexit functions, the modules' end; under -i"] [793 2 "// the REPL first (queue 289)"] [797 1 "// ExecModuleFile is ExecModule with __file__."] [819 1 "// runIn runs code as a module's body in the namespace g."] [822 44 "// an inlined comprehension's hidden locals"] [834 1 "// systemExitStatus is handle_system_exit's exit status (pythonrun.c): the exception's code (its one argument, the tuple"] [835 1 "// of several), None 0, an int as C's int (a value beyond long, or an int that wraps, -1: status 255), else its str on"] [836 1 "// stderr and 1 (